# large_field_literal_test.masm
#
# Exercises full-width 64-bit field-element literals expressed in
# hexadecimal form (`push.0x...`).  Miden's field is the prime field
# of order p = 2^64 - 2^32 + 1, so the largest representable element
# is `2^64 - 2^32 = 0xFFFFFFFE00000000`.  The recorder must preserve
# the full 64-bit precision when surfacing such a literal as a stack
# value -- a `i64` cast of that bit pattern is negative, so the
# recorder's `as_int() as i64` path round-trips it through the
# signed-integer ValueRecord without any string truncation.
#
# We push three literals so the test can pin all three on stack[0],
# stack[1] and stack[2] within a single step:
#
#   * push.0xFFFFFFFE00000000 -- the largest representable element
#                                (also the modulus minus 2^32; sits at
#                                the top of the prime field).
#   * push.0x100              -- a small hex literal (256).
#   * push.1234               -- a small decimal literal.

proc.lits.0
    push.0xFFFFFFFE00000000
    push.0x0100
    push.1234
end

begin
    # Leading push so #main is the first observed asmop context
    # and the recorder synthesises a register_call for it.
    push.0
    exec.lits
    drop drop drop drop
end
